WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.580
Matthew 27

00:02.580 --> 00:10.320
When morning came, all the chief priests and the elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death.

00:10.780 --> 00:15.320
And they bound him and led him away and delivered him over to Pilate the governor.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.960
Then when Judas, his betrayer, saw that Jesus was condemned,

00:20.440 --> 00:26.180
he changed his mind and brought back the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and the elders, saying,

00:26.760 --> 00:29.500
I have sinned by betraying innocent blood.

00:30.000 --> 00:30.960
They said,

00:31.640 --> 00:34.520
What is that to us? See to it yourself.

00:35.380 --> 00:41.740
And throwing down the pieces of silver into the temple, he departed, and he went and hanged himself.

00:42.080 --> 00:45.880
But the chief priests, taking the pieces of silver, said,

00:46.700 --> 00:51.900
It is not lawful to put them into the treasury, since it is blood money.

00:52.980 --> 00:59.400
So they took counsel and bought with them the potter's field as a burial place for strangers.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.820
Therefore that field has been called the field of blood to this day.

01:05.860 --> 01:10.080
Then was fulfilled what had been spoken by the prophet Jeremiah, saying,

01:10.880 --> 01:17.760
And they took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him on whom a price had been set by some of the sons of Israel,

01:17.940 --> 01:21.940
and they gave them for the potter's field, as the Lord directed me.

01:22.920 --> 01:27.000
Now Jesus stood before the governor, and the governor asked him,

01:27.000 --> 01:29.380
Are you the king of the Jews?

01:30.000 --> 01:30.840
Jesus said,

01:31.620 --> 01:32.760
You have said so.

01:33.520 --> 01:38.480
But when he was accused by the chief priests and elders, he gave no answer.

01:39.200 --> 01:40.600
Then Pilate said to him,

01:41.280 --> 01:44.680
Do you not hear how many things they testify against you?

01:45.360 --> 01:51.320
But he gave him no answer, not even to a single charge, so that the governor was greatly amazed.

01:51.780 --> 01:58.380
Now at the feast the governor was accustomed to release for the crowd any one prisoner whom they wanted.

01:59.060 --> 01:59.960
And they had then,

02:00.120 --> 02:02.380
a notorious prisoner called Barabbas.

02:02.880 --> 02:04.180
So when they had gathered,

02:04.540 --> 02:05.520
Pilate said to them,

02:06.340 --> 02:08.980
Whom do you want me to release for you,

02:09.220 --> 02:09.920
Barabbas,

02:10.200 --> 02:11.360
or Jesus,

02:11.740 --> 02:13.180
who is called Christ?

02:14.360 --> 02:18.020
For he knew that it was out of envy that they had delivered him up.

02:18.560 --> 02:18.960
Besides,

02:19.200 --> 02:21.120
while he was sitting on the judgment seat,

02:21.500 --> 02:23.300
his wife sent word to him,

02:23.640 --> 02:26.160
Have nothing to do with that righteous man,

02:26.880 --> 02:29.940
for I have suffered much because of him today in a dream,

02:30.120 --> 02:32.780
and I have not heard a word from him since the day of my death.

02:32.780 --> 02:36.780
Now the chief priests and the elders persuaded the crowd to ask for Barabbas and destroy Jesus.

02:36.780 --> 02:38.780
The governor again said to them,

02:38.780 --> 02:42.780
Which of the two do you want me to release for you?

02:42.780 --> 02:44.780
And they said,

02:44.780 --> 02:46.780
Barabbas!

02:46.780 --> 02:48.780
Pilate said to them,

02:48.780 --> 02:52.780
Then what shall I do with Jesus, who is called Christ?

02:52.780 --> 02:54.780
They all said,

02:54.780 --> 02:56.780
Let him be crucified!

02:56.780 --> 02:58.780
And he said,

02:58.780 --> 02:59.880
Why?

02:59.880 --> 03:01.880
What evil has he done?

03:01.880 --> 03:03.880
But they shouted all the more,

03:03.880 --> 03:07.880
Let him be crucified!

03:07.880 --> 03:10.880
So when Pilate saw that he was gaining nothing,

03:10.880 --> 03:12.880
but rather that a riot was beginning,

03:12.880 --> 03:16.880
he took water and washed his hands before the crowd, saying,

03:16.880 --> 03:19.880
I am innocent of this man's blood.

03:19.880 --> 03:21.880
See to it yourselves.

03:21.880 --> 03:23.880
And all the people answered,

03:23.880 --> 03:27.880
His blood be on us and on our children!

03:27.880 --> 03:29.880
Then he released for them Barabbas,

03:29.880 --> 03:32.880
and having scourged Jesus,

03:32.880 --> 03:35.880
delivered him to be crucified.

03:35.880 --> 03:39.880
Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the governor's headquarters,

03:39.880 --> 03:42.880
and they gathered the whole battalion before him.

03:42.880 --> 03:44.880
And they stripped him,

03:44.880 --> 03:46.880
and put a scarlet robe on him,

03:46.880 --> 03:48.880
and twisting together a crown of thorns,

03:48.880 --> 03:51.880
they put it on his head and put a reed in his right hand.

03:51.880 --> 03:55.880
And kneeling before him they mocked him, saying,

03:55.880 --> 03:57.880
Hail King of the Jews!

03:57.880 --> 04:00.880
Hail King of the Jews!

04:01.880 --> 04:03.880
And they spit on him,

04:03.880 --> 04:04.880
and took the reed,

04:04.880 --> 04:06.880
and struck him on the head.

04:06.880 --> 04:08.880
And when they had mocked him,

04:08.880 --> 04:10.880
they stripped him of the robe,

04:10.880 --> 04:12.880
and put his own clothes on him,

04:12.880 --> 04:14.880
and led him away to crucify him.

04:16.880 --> 04:17.880
As they went out,

04:17.880 --> 04:19.880
they found a man of Cyrene,

04:19.880 --> 04:20.880
Simon by name.

04:20.880 --> 04:23.880
They compelled this man to carry his cross.

04:23.880 --> 04:26.880
And when they came to a place called Golgotha,

04:26.880 --> 04:29.880
which means place of a skull,

04:29.880 --> 04:32.880
they offered him wine to drink mixed with gall.

04:32.880 --> 04:33.880
But when he tasted it,

04:33.880 --> 04:35.880
he would not drink it.

04:35.880 --> 04:37.880
And when they had crucified him,

04:37.880 --> 04:41.880
they divided his garments among them by casting lots.

04:41.880 --> 04:44.880
Then they sat down and kept watch over him there.

04:44.880 --> 04:47.880
And over his head they put the charge against him,

04:47.880 --> 04:48.880
which read,

04:48.880 --> 04:50.880
This is Jesus,

04:50.880 --> 04:53.880
the King of the Jews.

04:53.880 --> 04:55.880
Then two robbers were crucified with him,

04:55.880 --> 04:58.880
one on the right and one on the left.

04:58.880 --> 05:00.880
And those who passed by derided him,

05:00.880 --> 05:03.880
wagging their heads and saying,

05:03.880 --> 05:06.880
You who would destroy the temple

05:06.880 --> 05:09.880
and rebuild it in three days,

05:09.880 --> 05:11.880
save yourself.

05:11.880 --> 05:14.880
If you are the Son of God,

05:14.880 --> 05:16.880
come down from the cross.

05:16.880 --> 05:22.880
So also the chief priests with the scribes and elders mocked him, saying,

05:22.880 --> 05:24.880
He saved others.

05:24.880 --> 05:26.880
He cannot save himself.

05:26.880 --> 05:29.880
He is the King of Israel.

05:29.880 --> 05:31.880
Let him come down now from the cross,

05:31.880 --> 05:33.880
and we will believe in him.

05:33.880 --> 05:35.880
He trusts in God.

05:35.880 --> 05:38.880
Let God deliver him now if he desires him.

05:38.880 --> 05:39.880
For he said,

05:39.880 --> 05:42.880
I am the Son of God.

05:44.880 --> 05:46.880
And the robbers who were crucified with him

05:46.880 --> 05:49.880
also reviled him in the same way.

05:49.880 --> 05:51.880
Now from the sixth hour

05:51.880 --> 05:53.880
there was darkness over all the land

05:53.880 --> 05:55.880
until the ninth hour.

05:55.880 --> 05:57.880
And about the ninth hour

05:57.880 --> 06:02.880
Jesus cried out with a loud voice, saying,

06:02.880 --> 06:05.880
Eli!

06:05.880 --> 06:08.880
Eli!

06:08.880 --> 06:13.880
Lama sabachthani!

06:13.880 --> 06:16.880
That is,

06:16.880 --> 06:18.880
My God!

06:18.880 --> 06:21.880
My God!

06:21.880 --> 06:25.880
Why have you forsaken me?

06:25.880 --> 06:28.880
And some of the bystanders, hearing it, said,

06:28.880 --> 06:30.880
This man is calling Elijah.

06:30.880 --> 06:33.880
And one of them at once ran and took a sponge,

06:33.880 --> 06:35.880
filled it with sour wine,

06:35.880 --> 06:37.880
and put it on a reed,

06:37.880 --> 06:39.880
and gave it to him to drink.

06:39.880 --> 06:41.880
But the others said,

06:41.880 --> 06:42.880
Wait!

06:42.880 --> 06:45.880
Let us see whether Elijah will come to save him.

06:45.880 --> 06:49.880
And Jesus cried out again with a loud voice,

06:49.880 --> 06:52.880
and yielded up his spirit.

06:53.880 --> 06:55.880
And behold, the curtain of the temple

06:55.880 --> 06:58.880
was torn in two from top to bottom,

06:58.880 --> 07:01.880
and the earth shook, and the rocks were split.

07:01.880 --> 07:03.880
The tombs also were opened,

07:03.880 --> 07:05.880
and many bodies of the saints

07:05.880 --> 07:07.880
who had fallen asleep were raised.

07:07.880 --> 07:09.880
And coming out of the tombs after his resurrection,

07:09.880 --> 07:11.880
they went into the holy city

07:11.880 --> 07:13.880
and appeared to many.

07:13.880 --> 07:15.880
When the centurion and those who were with him,

07:15.880 --> 07:17.880
keeping watch over Jesus,

07:17.880 --> 07:19.880
saw the earthquake and what took place,

07:19.880 --> 07:22.880
they were filled with awe and said,

07:22.880 --> 07:26.880
Truly, this was the Son of God.

07:26.880 --> 07:28.880
There were also many women there,

07:28.880 --> 07:30.880
looking on from a distance,

07:30.880 --> 07:32.880
who had followed Jesus from Galilee,

07:32.880 --> 07:33.880
ministering to him,

07:33.880 --> 07:35.880
among whom were Mary Magdalene,

07:35.880 --> 07:38.880
and Mary the mother of James and Joseph,

07:38.880 --> 07:41.880
and the mother of the sons of Zebedee.

07:41.880 --> 07:43.880
When it was evening,

07:43.880 --> 07:45.880
there came a rich man from Arimathea,

07:45.880 --> 07:46.880
named Joseph,

07:46.880 --> 07:48.880
who also was a disciple of Jesus.

07:48.880 --> 07:51.880
He went to Pilate and asked for the body of Jesus.

07:51.880 --> 07:54.880
Then Pilate ordered it to be given to him.

07:54.880 --> 07:56.880
And Joseph took the body

07:56.880 --> 07:58.880
and wrapped it in a clean linen shroud,

07:58.880 --> 08:00.880
and laid it in his own new tomb,

08:00.880 --> 08:02.880
which he had cut in the rock.

08:02.880 --> 08:04.880
And he rolled a great stone

08:04.880 --> 08:06.880
to the entrance of the tomb

08:06.880 --> 08:08.880
and went away.

08:08.880 --> 08:10.880
Mary Magdalene and the other Mary were there,

08:10.880 --> 08:12.880
sitting opposite the tomb.

08:12.880 --> 08:14.880
The next day,

08:14.880 --> 08:15.880
that is,

08:15.880 --> 08:17.880
after the day of preparation,

08:17.880 --> 08:19.880
the chief priests and the Pharisees

08:19.880 --> 08:21.880
gathered before Pilate and said,

08:21.880 --> 08:22.880
Sir,

08:22.880 --> 08:25.880
we remember how that imposter said

08:25.880 --> 08:27.880
while he was still alive,

08:27.880 --> 08:30.880
After three days I will rise.

08:30.880 --> 08:32.880
Therefore,

08:32.880 --> 08:34.880
order the tomb to be made secure

08:34.880 --> 08:36.880
until the third day,

08:36.880 --> 08:39.880
lest his disciples go and steal him away

08:39.880 --> 08:41.880
and tell the people

08:41.880 --> 08:43.880
he has risen from the dead.

08:43.880 --> 08:45.880
And the last fraud,

08:45.880 --> 08:48.880
will be worse than the first.

08:48.880 --> 08:50.880
Pilate said to them,

08:50.880 --> 08:52.880
You have a guard of soldiers?

08:52.880 --> 08:55.880
Go, make it as secure as you can.

08:55.880 --> 08:57.880
So they went and made the tomb secure

08:57.880 --> 09:00.880
by sealing the stone and setting a guard.

